{"availability":"available","full":"pocket-nexus/quickjs-oxide","name":"quickjs-oxide","description":"An independent Rust rewrite of QuickJS targeting semantic feature parity","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":65,"forks":2,"created":"2026-07-10T18:47:53Z","updated":"2026-10-11T08:39:33Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pocket-nexus.github.io/quickjs-oxide/","topics":["javascript-engine","quickjs","rust"],"demo":"https://pocket-nexus.github.io/quickjs-oxide/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T04:14:56.264Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T04:14:56.264Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T04:14:56.264Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:01:04.187Z","stars":63,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-13T04:14:56.264Z","stars":65,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An unsafe-free Rust rewrite of QuickJS, targeting semantic Feature Parity with the official QuickJS 2026-06-04 release and its ES2025 behavior.","The engine is runnable, but it is not at Feature Parity yet. Implemented slices include binary data and Atomics, collections and weak references, Promise jobs, Unicode behavior, class elements, and static-module graphs with live bindings, top-level await, import attributes, JSON modules, import.meta, and dynamic import(). The Rust embedding API and file-module CLI also expose QuickJS's canonical, host-populated import.meta object. JavaScript-valued module-host errors retain their exact values and object/Symbol identity. Context-aware module-host callbacks can synchronously compile and return…","The authoritative R3fj Test262 baseline records 80,010 full-corpus passes out of 102,037 variants (78.413%), with 80,060 eligible variants (78.462%). The 80,010 / 80,060 runnable pass rate (99.938%) is a secondary quality measure, not the headline compatibility metric."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pocket-nexus/quickjs-oxide/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7